''   Updated.... 10 Sep 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================
''
''  This FILE is selected ONLY by compiling with -D BENCH_CFG (pnut-ts preprocessor
''  define). It is a peer of isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2, NOT a replacement for it:
''  isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 remains the one file end users edit. This file is
''  not user-editable configuration -- it is a fixed, plain statement of Stephen's
''  bench: the dual 6.5" wheel platform, two Rev B Universal Motor Driver boards,
''  18.5V pack (stated 2026-09-10). A fixed statement, never a choice made in this file. A second fixed
''  statement, the Doco bench (one DocoEng motor, one Rev A board, a told voltage), is selected by also
''  compiling with -D BENCH_DOCO and one DOCO_V* voltage symbol (tools/bench-run.sh).
''

CON { Hardware Description }

'  (1) Fixed CONSTANTS known by BLDC Motor Driver
'     --- DO NOT ADJUST ---

' Names of supported Motors
#0, MOTR_6_5_INCH, MOTR_DOCO_4KRPM

' Names of supported PinGroups
'   (added NO_USE) to make enum work, but you can't connect to it. ;-)
#0[8], PINS_P0_P15, PINS_P8_P23, PINS_P16_P31, PINS_NO_USE_P24_P39, PINS_P32_P47, PINS_P40_P55

' Names of supported voltages
#0, PWR_Unknown, PWR_6p0V, PWR_7p4V, PWR_11p1V, PWR_12p0V, PWR_14p8V, PWR_18p5V, PWR_22p2V, PWR_24p0V, PWR_25p9V
'  NOTE: Lipo battery sizes: 2s-7.4v, 3s-11.1v, 4s-14.8v, 5s-18.5v, 6s-22.2v, 7s-25.9v
'
' Board Detection Mode for BLDC driver boards
#30, BRD_AUTO_DET, BRD_REV_A, BRD_REV_B

' DEBUG output channels of isp_bldc_motor and isp_steering_2wheel (DEBUG[n]) -- mirrors
'   isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2; the masks are in the "DEBUG output" section below
#0, DBGCH_ERROR, DBGCH_WARNING, DBGCH_FAULT, DBGCH_LIFECYCLE, DBGCH_DETECT, DBGCH_COMMAND, DBGCH_SENSE, DBGCH_VALIDATE, DBGCH_TEST, DBGCH_HDMI_DUMP

'     --- DO NOT ADJUST ---

'   (2) The bench, as it actually is. TWO benches, each one fixed statement; -D BENCH_DOCO picks the Doco one:
'       - without it: the dual 6.5" wheel platform, two Rev B Universal Motor Driver boards, 18.5V pack,
'         Mini Edge Breakout Board (#64019)
'       - with -D BENCH_DOCO (and exactly one DOCO_V* voltage symbol, below): the Doco bench, one DocoEng 4k-rpm motor on one
'         Rev A board (STEPHEN 2026-10-03); tools/bench-run.sh chooses both symbols by NAME

#ifdef BENCH_DOCO

    MOTOR_TYPE = MOTR_DOCO_4KRPM

    ' one motor, on the P16 group (the Doco bench's board, as in the shipped single-motor configuration)
    ONLY_MOTOR_BASE = PINS_P16_P31

    ' The board is READ, never told (BRD_AUTO_DET). The Doco bench's board is a Rev A: EXPECTED_BOARD says so, for the
    '  harness to compare with what start() detected -- a run that reads anything else stops before it drives, and says so
    '  on screen and in the log (that check is the harness's; this file only states what the bench is).
    ONLY_BOARD_TYPE = BRD_AUTO_DET
    EXPECTED_BOARD = BRD_REV_A

    WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH = 0.0   ' no wheel attached (floating point constant)

    ' The shaft encoder's pins (A, B) are P48 and P49: reserved here (nothing else on this bench may use them).
    ENCODER_PIN_A = 48
    ENCODER_PIN_B = 49

    ' THE DRIVE VOLTAGE IS TOLD, NEVER SENSED: this bench has no pack sensor, so the voltage named at the command line is the
    '  only source there is. One DOCO_V* symbol per Doco voltage, given by tools/bench-run.sh from a voltage NAME (nothing is
    '  typed); DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV is the same voltage in millivolts, for every log banner to print.
#ifdef DOCO_V7P4
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_7p4V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 7_400
#elseifdef DOCO_V11P1
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_11p1V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 11_100
#elseifdef DOCO_V12P0
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_12p0V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 12_000
#elseifdef DOCO_V14P8
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_14p8V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 14_800
#elseifdef DOCO_V18P5
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_18p5V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 18_500
#elseifdef DOCO_V22P2
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_22p2V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 22_200
#elseifdef DOCO_V24P0
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_24p0V
    DRIVE_VOLTAGE_TOLD_MV = 24_000
#else
#ifdef __PNUT_TS__
#ERROR No Doco voltage selected: -D BENCH_DOCO needs one of -D DOCO_V7P4, DOCO_V11P1, DOCO_V12P0, DOCO_V14P8, DOCO_V18P5, DOCO_V22P2, DOCO_V24P0 (tools/bench-run.sh gives it, from the tier's voltage name)
#endif
#endif

    ' ---- a check of the pin group above, as in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (do not edit). If the compiler stops on the
    '  CHECK_ line below with "Divide by zero", its comment says what to change.
    ONLY_IS_A_PIN_GROUP = (ONLY_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P0_P15) or (ONLY_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P8_P23) or (ONLY_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P16_P31) or (ONLY_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P32_P47) or (ONLY_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P40_P55)
    CHECK_ONLY_PIN_GROUP = 1 / -ONLY_IS_A_PIN_GROUP     ' ONLY_MOTOR_BASE is not a pin group: use PINS_P0_P15, PINS_P8_P23, PINS_P16_P31, PINS_P32_P47 or PINS_P40_P55

#else

    MOTOR_TYPE = MOTR_6_5_INCH

    ' BOTH the Rev A and the Rev B platform use this SAME pin mapping (Stephen, 2026-09-11),
    ' so the A/B detection comparison is like-for-like and needs no per-rig change. It also
    ' means P28 and P44 are gate-driver inputs on BOTH rigs, not just this one.
    ' PROVENANCE: MEASURED at the bench 2026-09-11, and confirmed by test_bench_spin.spin2
    ' turning both wheels. These were WRONG until then -- the file was created by copying the
    ' first dual block of the shipped user config (LEFT = PINS_P0_P15) and labelling the result
    ' "the bench, as it actually is", which it was not. The 14:39 Tier 0 log had already read
    ' "Board not detected!" on P0_P15 and "64010 Rev B" on P32_P47; that was believed to be a
    ' detection defect rather than a wrong declaration, and a fabricated finding propagated into
    ' two task bodies before it was caught. Do not change these without a bench run that shows
    ' both wheels turning, and update this note with the date when you do.
    LEFT_MOTOR_BASE = PINS_P32_P47
    RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE = PINS_P16_P31

    DRIVE_VOLTAGE = PWR_18p5V

    WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH = 6.5   ' 6.5 inches (floating point constant)

    LEFT_BOARD_TYPE = BRD_AUTO_DET
    RIGHT_BOARD_TYPE = BRD_AUTO_DET

    ' ---- checks of the pin groups above, as in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2 (do not edit). If the
    '  compiler stops on a CHECK_ line below with "Divide by zero", that line's comment says what to change.
    LEFT_IS_A_PIN_GROUP = (LEFT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P0_P15) or (LEFT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P8_P23) or (LEFT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P16_P31) or (LEFT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P32_P47) or (LEFT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P40_P55)
    RIGHT_IS_A_PIN_GROUP = (RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P0_P15) or (RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P8_P23) or (RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P16_P31) or (RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P32_P47) or (RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE == PINS_P40_P55)
    GROUPS_DO_NOT_OVERLAP = abs (LEFT_MOTOR_BASE - RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE) >= 16       ' a board uses its base pin and the 15 above it
    CHECK_LEFT_PIN_GROUP = 1 / -LEFT_IS_A_PIN_GROUP     ' LEFT_MOTOR_BASE is not a pin group: use PINS_P0_P15, PINS_P8_P23, PINS_P16_P31, PINS_P32_P47 or PINS_P40_P55
    CHECK_RIGHT_PIN_GROUP = 1 / -RIGHT_IS_A_PIN_GROUP   ' RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE is not a pin group: use PINS_P0_P15, PINS_P8_P23, PINS_P16_P31, PINS_P32_P47 or PINS_P40_P55
    CHECK_GROUPS_APART = 1 / -GROUPS_DO_NOT_OVERLAP     ' LEFT_MOTOR_BASE and RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE share pins: pick two groups whose pin ranges do not overlap (e.g. PINS_P16_P31 and PINS_P32_P47)

#endif

CON { DEBUG output }

'  Mirrors isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2's defaults, so a bench build prints what it printed
'   before DEBUG channels. A bench binary that needs a quieter set changes these in its own task.

#ifdef BENCH_QUIET
    ' motion harness (task 3508): no debug() reachable from any cog a library stop() can end
    MOTOR_DBG_MASK = DECOD DBGCH_ERROR | DECOD DBGCH_WARNING
    STEER_DBG_MASK = DECOD DBGCH_ERROR | DECOD DBGCH_WARNING
#else
    MOTOR_DBG_MASK = DECOD DBGCH_ERROR | DECOD DBGCH_WARNING | DECOD DBGCH_FAULT | DECOD DBGCH_LIFECYCLE | DECOD DBGCH_DETECT | DECOD DBGCH_COMMAND | DECOD DBGCH_SENSE | DECOD DBGCH_VALIDATE | DECOD DBGCH_TEST
    STEER_DBG_MASK = DECOD DBGCH_ERROR | DECOD DBGCH_WARNING | DECOD DBGCH_FAULT | DECOD DBGCH_LIFECYCLE | DECOD DBGCH_DETECT | DECOD DBGCH_COMMAND | DECOD DBGCH_SENSE | DECOD DBGCH_VALIDATE | DECOD DBGCH_TEST
#endif

CON { pack voltage sensor }

'  Stephen's unit, fitted 2026-09-26 on P0 (clear of both motor groups, P16-P47; the HDMI demos' P0-P7 adapter
'   cannot share this rig). Parts as measured: R1 68.0k, R3 0.999k, R2 9.99k, R4 1.003M, so with R4's loading
'   pack = pin x 7.882, against the driver's nominal 7.81: CAL_PERMILLE ~1009 DERIVED from the resistors. The
'   one-time meter calibration (dual-pack) sets the value; 1009 was its prediction.
'  CALIBRATED 2026-09-26 (dual-pack, debug_260926-163930.log): DMM 20_740 mV at the Powerpole against the driver's
'   uncalibrated 20_488 mV -> 1000 x 20_740 / 20_488 = 1012. The 0.3 % beyond the resistor prediction is 8 mV at the
'   pin, the P2 pin ADC's documented offset (P2AN001, <= 9 mV).
#ifdef BENCH_DOCO
'  The Doco bench has no pack sensor (the voltage is told, see DRIVE_VOLTAGE above): not fitted, and the pin and calibration
'   below are ignored when it is not.
    PACK_SENSOR_FITTED = FALSE
    PACK_SENSE_PIN = 0
    PACK_SENSE_CAL_PERMILLE = 1000
#else
    PACK_SENSOR_FITTED = TRUE
    PACK_SENSE_PIN = 0
    PACK_SENSE_CAL_PERMILLE = 1012
#endif

PUB null()      ' This is not a top level object

CON { license }

